his is not \"drift\", this text was never the binary's output):\n  grep -rn \"opt-in --record PATH appends\" lore/            -> no match at HEAD\n  git log --oneline -S\"opt-in --record PATH appends\" -- lore/__main__.py   -> EMPTY (no revision ever contained it)\n  grep -rn \"catch-all bucket is marked\" lore/              -> no match at HEAD\n  git log --oneline -S\"catch-all bucket is marked\" -- lore/__main__.py     -> EMPTY\nSo INSTALL's block was hand-edited; a reader who runs the documented command and diffs sees a doc/binary mismatch and reasonably suspects their install.\n\nFACTS BEHIND THE INSERTED TEXT ARE REAL — keep them, move them out of the fence:\n- `--record` is a real, shipped flag; its own help lives in `lore gate --help` (lore/__main__.py:862 \"REVIEW-LORE-001 OPT-IN: append one durable JSONL audit record\") and in prose at README.md:245-248 and docs/INSTALL.md:384-390.\n- The bucket marker is real for the table and json renderers; the md renderer gap is ALREADY OWNED by pending row README-3 — do not re-handle it here.\n\nFIX (one sitting, docs/INSTALL.md only):\n1. Re-paste the true `uv run python -m lore --help` output verbatim into the fence at docs/INSTALL.md:116-147 (the eight-verb list is unchanged and correct).\n2. If the --record / bucket detail is worth keeping in that section, put it as prose BELOW the fence (reuse the existing README.md:245-248 and README.md:395-403 wording) — never inside a block presented as command output.\n\nACCEPTANCE (reviewer's falsifiable test): `uv run python -m lore --help` writes to a file and `diff` against the fenced block in docs/INSTALL.md is EMPTY; and no sentence inside that fence is absent from the binary's own output (checked by the same diff).\n\nch:trace row=DOC-5 spec=docs/INSTALL.md#the-help-the-whole-shipped-surface test=none:no-test-covers-pasted-help-fidelity doc=docs/INSTALL.md#L116 evidence=/home/kara/.hermes/stand-in/docs/lore/audit-lore-docs-2026-10-19-21-37-57.md witness=none:cli-help-ou