+ {"id": "PERF-2", "title": "[P3] `lore audit` re-reads and re-parses the ENTIRE validate-history ledger once per registry class (14 full passes): 144 ms at today's 3,161-row ledger, 1.06 s at 10x, 9.56 s at 100x \u2014 a single pass is 3.8x (10x: 11.5x) cheaper for the same rows", "status": "complete", "priority": "P3", "created_by": "lore-dogfood-run14", "reasoning": "MEASURED at HEAD a6984b4 on the control box (loadavg 2.9-4.6), the repo's own live ledger as the input: .lore/validate-history.jsonl = 3,161 rows / 878,746 bytes / 18 days / ~176 rows written per day by this product's own `validate --execute` (census: docs/qa/evidence/run14/ledger-census.txt). Rows were resized in scratch dirs (builder /tmp/lore-df14/mkhistory.py) keeping the exact record shape.\n\nCOMMAND (hyperfine --warmup 3 --runs 12, cwd = the dir holding ./.lore/validate-history.jsonl), HEAD build:\n  <repo>/.venv/bin/python -m lore audit\n  ledger rows       audit mean +- sigma     consult (same ledger)\n  0 (no ledger)     48.3 ms +-  2.5 ms      53.9 ms +- 5.5 ms\n  3,161 (today)    144.2 ms +- 15.7 ms      59.4 ms +- 3.1 ms\n  31,610 (10x)       1.056 s +- 0.151 s    116.8 ms +- 4.9 ms\n  316,100 (100x)     9.564 s +- 0.388 s    not measured (--runs 3)\nCOLD (sync + /proc/sys/vm/drop_caches before each run, 3,161-row ledger): audit real 0.23 s / 0.24 s vs warm 0.13 s; consult cold 0.15 s vs warm 0.05 s; control cold `cat` of the ledger 0.03 s. The ledger-dependent part is therefore ~88 ms warm today and ~1.0 s at 10x.\n\nPROFILE (cProfile -s tottime -m lore audit, 3,161-row ledger): __main__.py:560(_audit_rows) 0.200 s cum; validate.py:1194(last_local_validation) called 14 times, 44,254 json.loads, 14 readlines(). At 31,610 rows the same call site reads 1.974 s cum / 442,540 json.loads \u2014 i.e. 14 full copies of the file parsed per audit, and the parse work IS the cost.\n\nHOT PATH: lore/__main__.py:604 (`rec = last_local_validation(rb.class_id, path=history_path)` inside the one-row-per