onl` on the bucket line printing 0. Curated classes' records stay byte-identical (`head`-snapshot equality); a test pins the chosen shape; quote the scratch evidence."}
+ {"id": "LORE-063-R2", "title": "[P3] recurrence of LORE-063: skills/lore-usage/SKILL.md:123 read 'expect: 510 passed' while canonical is 523, and `count_sweep.py 523 .` still exits 0 \u2014 the self-reference exemption (count_sweep.py:102-103) exempts the ONE line whose job is to state the count, so this drifted again after its fix", "status": "complete", "priority": "P3", "created_by": "lore-dogfood-run14", "reasoning": "RECURRENCE of LORE-063 (closed complete, fix commit 615fda1) at HEAD a6984b4. The row's own title named BOTH halves; only one was fixed.\n\nLIVE REPRO (control box, 2026-10-20):\n  $ .venv/bin/python -m pytest -q | tail -1\n  523 passed in 4.59s\n  $ cat scripts/test-count.txt\n  523\n  $ grep -n 'expect:' skills/lore-usage/SKILL.md\n  123:uv run pytest -q    # expect: 510 passed (count synced to scripts/test-count.txt, LORE-029)\n  $ .venv/bin/python scripts/count_sweep.py 523 .\n  count_sweep_rc=0            # <-- the guard reports CLEAN while the line reads 510 vs 523\n\nMECHANISM (still live, code unchanged): scripts/count_sweep.py:102-103 exempts a whole LINE from the test-count family as soon as `SELF_REFERENCE = \"scripts/test-count.txt\"` appears anywhere in it. The skill's line 123 both quotes the sync file AND asserts a number \u2014 so the one line whose whole purpose is to state the canonical count is the one line the guard cannot check. `count_sweep.py` has not been touched since 3f435ed (2026-09-26, LORE-036); `git log -1 -S'SELF_REFERENCE' -- scripts/count_sweep.py` = 3f435ed, i.e. no fix for the exemption ever landed.\n\nWHY THE CLOSURE DID NOT HOLD: LORE-063's foreman_note reads \"skill line 123 updated 463->510 ... Count guard PASS\". The PASS was the guard's normal output on the exemption it never evaluates \u2014 the number was synced at 510 while canonical was 510, and then 13 tests were added (510 -> 523) and the doc silently rotted again. The drift was caught this run by hand, not by the guard: `count_sweep.py 523 .` return